# Known answers of Go 1.24's math/big.Float (rounding mode ToNearestEven), one case per line:
#   op zprec xprec x [yprec y] -> result
# with every float in Go's Text('p', 0) form ("0", "-0", "[-]0x.<hex>p<exp>", the value 0.<hex> * 2^exp). A selection
# of cancellations, exact ties, results that carry into a new bit, zeros and signs, far-apart exponents, mixed
# precisions and random operands at 53, 64, 318, 574 and 1000 bits; Float64 at the edges (ties, denormals, the range's
# ends), SetFloat64, SetString of cosine_approx's digits of pi, and round(x * 2^bits) with the halves away from zero
# (BigFloat.to_fixed; Go's reference computed it with big.Int).
